Repository: <workspace> own EXACTLY ONE FILE: src/context.ts. Do not modify any other file. Do not run git add/stage/commit.

Task: Fix the `res` setter (currently lines 414-434) so that when a response is already set on the context (e.g. middleware set a cookie via `c.res`/`c.header`) and a new Response is assigned with its own `Set-Cookie` header(s), BOTH the previous cookies and the new response's cookies survive. Today the setter does `_res.headers.delete('set-cookie')` then appends only the previous cookies, dropping the new response's cookies.

Required semantics (this is the contract another agent's tests rely on):
1. Keep the existing behavior of copying previous headers onto the new response, skipping `content-type`.
2. For `set-cookie`, do NOT overwrite/drop the new response's cookies.
3. Resulting cookie order must be: previous cookies first (in their original order), then the new response's cookies (in their original order).
4. Avoid duplicate appends: handle `set-cookie` outside the generic header loop (skip `k === 'set-cookie'` in the loop), read previous cookies with `this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()`, read new cookies with `_res.headers.getSetCookie()`, and only if there is at least one cookie delete `set-cookie` from the freshly-created `_res` and re-append `[...previousCookies, ...newCookies]`.
5. Preserve all existing behavior when either `this.#res` or `_res` is undefined, including `this.#res = _res; this.finalized = true`.
6. Keep the `createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)` re-creation so the headers are mutable.

Implementation shape (adapt as needed but keep it minimal and typed):
```ts
set res(_res: Response | undefined) {
  if (this.#res && _res) {
    _res = createResponseInstance(_res.body, _res)
    const prevCookies = this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()
    for (const [k, v] of this.#res.headers.entries()) {
      if (k === 'content-type' || k === 'set-cookie') {
        continue
      }
      _res.headers.set(k, v)
    }
    if (prevCookies.length) {
      const newCookies = _res.headers.getSetCookie()
      _res.headers.delete('set-cookie')
      for (const cookie of [...prevCookies, ...newCookies]) {
        _res.headers.append('set-cookie', cookie)
      }
    }
  }
  this.#res = _res
  this.finalized = true
}
```

Keep formatting/lint style of the repo (prettier-ish, no semicolons). Do not change public API or unrelated logic. Do not run the test suite (the coordinator will run it after both agents finish). Report the exact diff you applied.

